{title: 139 - While Shepherds Watched Their Flocks}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #139 • WINCHESTER OLD • 9.5.8.6}
{lyricist: Nahum Tate}
{composer: Este's Psalter}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 139}
{meta: tune WINCHESTER OLD}
{meta: meter 9.5.8.6}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm/A]While [F/C]shepherds [Bb]watched their [C]flocks [F/C]by [C]night,
[Dm]All seated [C]onthe ground,
[F/C]The [Bb]angel of [F/C]the [C]Lord [Dm/A]came [Am]down,
[Am]And [C]glory [Bb]shone [C/G]around.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm/A]"Fear [F/C]nor!" [C]said [Dm/A]he- [Bb/D]for [F/C]mighty [C]dread
[Dm]Had seized their [C]troubled mind-
[F/C]"Glad [Bb]tidings of [F/C]great [C]joy [Dm/A]I [Am]bring,
[Am]To [C]you [Dm/A]and [Bb]all [C/G]mankind.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm/A]"To [F/C]you, [C]in [Dm/A]David's [F/C]town this [C]day,
[Dm]Is born of [C]David's line,
[F/C]The [Bb]Savior who [F/C]is [C]Christ [Dm/A]the [Am]Lord;
[Am]And [C]this [Dm/A]shall [Bb]be [C/G]the [Dm/A]sign:
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm/A]"The [F/C]heavenly [Bb]Babe you [C]there [F/C]shall [C]find
[Dm]To human [C]view displayed,
[F/C]All [Bb]meanly wrapped [F/C]in [C]swathing [Am]bands,
[Am]And [C]in [Dm/A]a [Bb]manger [Dm/A]laid."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Dm/A]Thus [F/C]spake [C]the [Dm/A]seraph; [F/C]and forth [C]with
[Dm]Appeared a [C]shining throng
[F/C]Of [Bb]angels praising [C]God [Dm/A]on [Am]high,
[Am]Who [C]thus [Dm/A]addressed [C/G]their [Dm/A]song:
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[Dm/A]"All [F/C]glory [Dm/A]be [Bb/D]to [F/C]God on [C]high,
[Dm]And to the [C]earth be peace;
[F/C]Good will [Bb]henceforth [F/C]from heaven [Dm/A]to [Am]men,
[Am]Begin [Dm/A]and [Bb]never [Dm/A]cease!"
{end_of_verse}
